# Copy to .env and set for this machine. Not committed.
#
# RPE_DATA_ROOT is the pipeline tree holding Inputs/, Outputs/ and Build Artifacts/.
# It differs per machine and must never be hardcoded in the build code — see
# build/rpe_env.py. Repointing this line is the ONLY change a new machine needs.

# The pipeline root is the CSM_Reporting folder on the CSI share (Aaron,
# 2026-09-14): one place for every CSM's imports, exports and project files. It
# needs the VPN off-site. There is no separate backup copy of this tree, and
# nothing syncs it anywhere: the ORIGINAL SOURCES are the backup. Every input can
# be re-fetched — the CSI shares hold the ODD extracts, DCOs, ARS workbooks and
# MRPCPM analyses, and the mailbox holds the MRPC / CashPlease reports and the ICS
# workbooks. `scripts/watch_sources.py --copy --mail` is how they come back.

# --- Every machine ---
RPE_DATA_ROOT=\\PADMIS105\Velocity_company\CSM_Reporting

# --- History: C:\Data Pipelines\RPE Pipeline (2026-09-09 to 2026-09-14) ---
# The previous local root. C:\Data Pipelines\ also holds "Renewals Pipeline", a
# DIFFERENT project with its own Inputs\ and Outputs\. A wrong root fails loudly —
# rpe_env.data_root() raises on a path that is not a directory.

# --- The CSI source shares (all need the VPN) ---
# These are where the data team LANDS files; scripts/watch_sources.py copies from
# them into Inputs/. They are separate from RPE_DATA_ROOT and default to the paths
# in scripts/deck_status.py — set these only to override.
# ODD extracts land in each CSM's own folder (2026-09-14): "CSM=path" entries
# separated by ";". A single bare path still works.
# RPE_SRC_ODDD=Aaron Burgard=\\PADMIS105\Velocity_company\Aburgard\ODDD;Daniel Wood=\\PADMIS105\Velocity_company\Dan Wood\OD Data Dumps;Gregg Miller=\\PADMIS105\Velocity_company\GMiller\OD Data Dumps;James Gilmore=\\PADMIS105\Velocity_company\JamesG\OD Data Dumps;Jordan Berkowitz=\\PADMIS105\Velocity_company\JBerkowitz\OD Data Dumps
# RPE_SRC_REPORTS=\\PADMIS105\Velocity_clientreports
